    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Trea Turner** (77.53) and **Kyle Schwarber** (76.68), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) despite facing a moderate arm in Bradish. **Yordan Alvarez** (73.79) remains a must-start given his elite xwOBA of 0.476, though his ceiling is slightly capped by a modest park factor compared to our leadoff duo. We are also capitalizing on high-efficiency platoon advantages today; **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) is a strong play against the fading Scherzer, where a combination of a +19% SP skill edge and a +11% platoon boost elevates his output well above his base projection. Similarly, **Dillon Dingler** (62.06) is primed to take advantage of his dynamic platoon split against the lefty Jump, providing necessary stability behind the plate.\n\nRegarding roster management, the most difficult decision involved keeping **Chase Meidroth** (36.63) on the bench. While his underlying metrics are serviceable, the combination of a negative park factor and an unfavorable batting order position (7th) dropped him well below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" We are prioritizing the stolen base potential and higher volatility of our active lineup to chase upside in a tight Roto race. Risks remain for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.35); while his matchup against Cole presents a challenging strikeout threat, his leadoff spot and platoon advantage against a righty are essential for our stolen base targets. Owners should monitor weather updates regarding \"Wind In\" flags for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, which could dampen his power profile today. Finally, we remain cautious regarding the bench status of **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith**, both of whom remain sidelined for this matchup, keeping our bench depth clear of active rotation candidates.",
